About WPP Media

WPP is the creative transformation company. We use the power of creativity to build better futures for our people, planet, clients and communities. For more information, visit wpp.com.

WPP Media is WPP’s global media collective. In a world where media is everywhere and in everything, we bring the best platform, people, and partners together to create limitless opportunities for growth. For more information, visit wppmedia.com

At WPP Media, we believe in the power of our culture and our people. It’s what elevates us to deliver exceptional experiences for both our clients and each other. In this role it will be critical to embrace WPP &amp; WPP Media’s shared core values:

• Be Extraordinary by Leading Collectively to Inspire transformational Creativity.

• Create an Open environment by Balancing People and Client Experiences by Cultivating Trust .

• Lead Optimistically by Championing Growth and Development to Mobilize the Enterprise .

Role Summary and Impact

The Manager, Resource Management is responsible for &nbsp;aligning capabilities with client needs to ensure&nbsp; timely &nbsp;and effective fulfillment of roles. This position plays a critical role in advising client teams on fulfillment timelines, staff planning, and role expectations, while&nbsp; maintaining &nbsp; accurate &nbsp;data. The Capacity Planner navigates between various fulfillment channels to&nbsp; optimize team configurations and enhance client strategies.

Skills and Experience

• Aligned to a book of business, agency, and/or group of accounts &nbsp;

• Advise client teams on fulfillment timelines to ensure client readiness and success &nbsp;

• Advise client teams on roles expectations and recommendations against staff plans &nbsp;

• Own and drive data accuracy used for Workforce Planning&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Pivot between fulfilment channels and understand skills needed to plan client strategies (Talent Acquisition/ Contracting/Resource Management) &nbsp;

• Collaborate with client teams to ensure Staff Plans are accurate and always maintained &nbsp;

• Works to assemble and optimize the best possible team for our clients &nbsp;

• Ensure the fulfillment of staff plans across internal and external supply &nbsp;

• Simplify client team interactions; facilitating and aggregating all needs between our Resource Management and Talent Acquisition functions (including contract &amp; offshore needs) &nbsp;

• Partner with Workforce Planning to provide client demand input to shape current &amp; future demand predictions and strategies

• Act as a central point of contact for client teams, simplifying communication and ensuring clarity in staffing requirements &nbsp;

• Continuously assess and refine the staffing fulfillment process to enhance efficiency, minimize bottlenecks, and improve the overall client experience &nbsp;

• Monitor and track the progress of fulfillment activities, ensuring alignment with the client's needs and strategic goals &nbsp;

• Utilize data and analytics to measure the effectiveness of the fulfillment plan, making data-driven decisions to optimize staffing levels

• Develop a deep understanding of client needs, expectations, and existing staff plans &nbsp;

• Leverage knowledge of Resource Management, Workforce Planning, and staffing solutions and utilize expertise

Principal Product Manager (AI Product) - Join Our Innovative Team at think-cell Software &nbsp;

Our Story &nbsp;

At think-cell, we create powerful software solutions that help professionals be more efficient and productive. Founded in 2002 and based in Berlin, our tools integrate seamlessly with Microsoft Office to help users create presentations, charts, and diagrams with ease. Our dynamic, international team values creativity, collaboration, and technical excellence. &nbsp;

What You Will Do   &nbsp;

You'll co- own our AI product end-to-end, from discovery to business outcome . You'll set direction&l

Who we are

About Stripe&nbsp;

Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone's reach while doing the most important work of your career.

What you’ll do

Responsibilities

• Develop scalable computer systems that manage a large volume of information and use them to fulfill business goals for Stripe and its partners.&nbsp;

• Design, implement and deploy adaptable rules systems that use this information to output internal assessments, perform scoring, and derive automated actions for mitigating financial risk and increase the efficiency of Stripe’s global risk mitigation program.&nbsp;

• Design and build tools that ingest and process signals from various sources to make them more accessible for our partner teams.&nbsp;

• Participate in all parts of the software development workflow and see the projects through to completion, including their large-scale deployment.&nbsp;

• Improve engineering standards, tooling, and processes.&nbsp;

• Debug production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack.&nbsp;

• Design, build, and maintain APIs, services, and systems across Stripe’s engineering teams.

Who you are

Minimum requirements

Bachelor’s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field plus 4 years of experience in Software Development or a related occupation. Employer is willing to accept a 3 or 4 year US or foreign degree.

Must also have 4 years of experience in each of the following:

• Building software solutions in Python, Ruby, Objective C, C++, or similar;

• Designing, building, and maintaining scalable systems;

• Translating business needs into software requirements and designs;

• Debugging production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack; and,

• Distributed systems.

Salary: $173,000 - $259,600/yr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.

40 hrs/week

50% telecommuting permitted.

Multiple Positions Available.&nbsp;

